## Installation

Steps 1 and 2 are what MACRO_INLINE_CODE make install MACRO_INLINE_CODE does for you, so run that instead if you
like. Step 3 is on you either way.

**1. Put the binary on your PATH.** The build leaves it at MACRO_INLINE_CODE build/_tec MACRO_INLINE_CODE ; move
it into one of the directories listed in MACRO_INLINE_CODE PATH MACRO_INLINE_CODE — MACRO_INLINE_CODE ~/.local/bin MACRO_INLINE_CODE is a
good spot.

**2. Add the shell wrapper** to your shell rc file, whether that is
MACRO_INLINE_CODE ~/.bashrc MACRO_INLINE_CODE , MACRO_INLINE_CODE ~/.zshrc MACRO_INLINE_CODE or another one. The wrapper is what allows
Tec to change the working directory of your current shell.

MACRO_CODE bash
include(shell/tec.sh)dnl
MACRO_CODE

**3. Create a config file**, either at MACRO_INLINE_CODE ~/.tec/tec.cfg MACRO_INLINE_CODE or at
MACRO_INLINE_CODE ~/.config/tec/tec.cfg MACRO_INLINE_CODE , and fill it with the content below. Tec reads the
first of the two it finds, or the one passed with MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec -f PATH MACRO_INLINE_CODE .

MACRO_CODE
include(shell/tec.cfg)dnl
MACRO_CODE

