## Plugins

Plugins are installed by MACRO_INLINE_CODE nine MACRO_INLINE_CODE , the Tec plugin manager. To get it:

MACRO_CODE bash
PGNDIR="$HOME/.local/lib/tec/pgn"
git clone https://github.com/roachme/tec-nine.git "$PGNDIR/nine"
MACRO_CODE

Two things to keep in mind, here and for every other plugin:

- the repo directory name carries **no** MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec- MACRO_INLINE_CODE prefix;
- MACRO_INLINE_CODE PGNDIR MACRO_INLINE_CODE has to match MACRO_INLINE_CODE base.pgn MACRO_INLINE_CODE from the MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec.cfg MACRO_INLINE_CODE shown above.

That is the whole mechanism: an executable at MACRO_INLINE_CODE base.pgn/NAME/NAME MACRO_INLINE_CODE is run by
MACRO_INLINE_CODE tec NAME MACRO_INLINE_CODE , and hooks can call it for you.

A few worth a look:

| Plugin | What it does |
| :-- | :-- |
| [nine](https://github.com/roachme/tec-nine.git) | Tec plugin manager |
| [gmux](https://github.com/roachme/tec-gmux.git) | Manage a bunch of git repos |
| [find](https://github.com/roachme/tec-find.git) | Find stuff in tasks |
| [conv](https://github.com/roachme/tec-conv.git) | Workflow engine: kanban and custom workflows |

Each of them carries setup notes of its own, so read its README before use.

